                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Experienced on the Oculus Quest 2[/h1]\n\nI know most people don't like endless runners. I happen to like good VR endless runners. However, this one isn't one of them. It's pretty bad and very basic. Gaze-based navigation only. Don't use motion controllers at all. There are 3 very short stages only that repeat often and the gaps you can go through get smaller and you'll go faster. That's the whole game. \n\nTwo of the Three stages are very ugly looking (pizza tunnel and blood vessel tunnel). You'll probably get neck strain. You'll soon grow to dislike the music. I just wanted to quit after 10 minutes. I couldn't take it anymore.\n\nI paid .74 cents for this. I still feel ripped off. This should be free to play. It is not worth anything. \n\n[b]Rate 3/10. Dev, you should be ashamed for actually asking money for this low-effort product. Shame on you.[/b]",
